(6380287, 945250, 63218, '<td valign="top">I enjoy the moment of discovery, when the ''blurry mess'' suddenly resolves itself &amp; I see. But how in the world did you get a little French Bulldog to wear that hat?  <b><i>Just kidding!!!</i></b> This looks like it might be the kitteh''s favorite piece of furniture. Bless its little furry head.</td>', 'I enjoy the moment of discovery, when the ''blurry mess'' suddenly resolves itself & I see. But how in the world did you get a little French Bulldog to wear that hat?  Just kidding!!! This looks like it might be the kitteh''s favorite piece of furniture. Bless its little furry head.', '2011-04-09 11:33:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380337, 945245, 15711, '<td valign="top">Quite avant garde.  He almost appears to be floating on that grass. Interesting and thoughtful take on the challenge. :)  Coming back.  I''m having a hard time with this voting thing.  Maybe I am trying way too hard.  Is this more contemporary art or fine art?  It is quite thought provoking and executed in a way to make us take more than one look.  For that, I''m upping the score.</td>', 'Quite avant garde.  He almost appears to be floating on that grass. Interesting and thoughtful take on the challenge. :)  Coming back.  I''m having a hard time with this voting thing.  Maybe I am trying way too hard.  Is this more contemporary art or fine art?  It is quite thought provoking and executed in a way to make us take more than one look.  For that, I''m upping the score.', '2011-04-09 12:11:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380338, 945083, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''ve come back to this several times.  Fine art?  Hmmmm not sure, but that is so subjective.  I think it speaks of our society in general and if that is commentary and makes us think, then art it is.  I''m thinking contemporary more than ''fine'' if that makes any sense at all.</td>', 'I''ve come back to this several times.  Fine art?  Hmmmm not sure, but that is so subjective.  I think it speaks of our society in general and if that is commentary and makes us think, then art it is.  I''m thinking contemporary more than ''fine'' if that makes any sense at all.', '2011-04-09 12:13:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380341, 945175, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''ve come back to this several times.  I''m struggling with so many of these images to be considered ''fine art."  Is it a good photo?  yes  Do I think it deserves an above average score? yes  Is it fine art?  Not so sure. (IMHO) 6</td>', 'I''ve come back to this several times.  I''m struggling with so many of these images to be considered ''fine art."  Is it a good photo?  yes  Do I think it deserves an above average score? yes  Is it fine art?  Not so sure. (IMHO) 6', '2011-04-09 12:15:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380346, 945244, 15711, '<td valign="top">This could tell a story.  It could be an example of social commentary of the day.  Fine art?  I''m not so sure.  But as I struggle with so many of these images, I realize how subjective this whole subject is.  I think I''ll stick with my first gut reaction. 6 I like how the light above the roof of the doorway mimics the light on the guy''s head and arms.  Almost like the same shape as the doorway in miniature.</td>', 'This could tell a story.  It could be an example of social commentary of the day.  Fine art?  I''m not so sure.  But as I struggle with so many of these images, I realize how subjective this whole subject is.  I think I''ll stick with my first gut reaction. 6 I like how the light above the roof of the doorway mimics the light on the guy''s head and arms.  Almost like the same shape as the doorway in miniature.', '2011-04-09 12:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380350, 944750, 63218, '<td valign="top">I like this, it looks to me like the details of what''s there have been sacrificed to the truth of what''s there.  The truth of it escapes my mental grasp, as usual, but I can sense its presence. Well done. The texture details in the FG are sensually pleasurable to look at, I want to reach out &amp; touch.</td>', 'I like this, it looks to me like the details of what''s there have been sacrificed to the truth of what''s there.  The truth of it escapes my mental grasp, as usual, but I can sense its presence. Well done. The texture details in the FG are sensually pleasurable to look at, I want to reach out & touch.', '2011-04-09 12:18:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380351, 944059, 15711, '<td valign="top">Is that Freddy Krueger in the lower left? LOL I like the tulip theme that runs throughout.  This is bizarre and certainly befitting of the Fine Art category.  I can see this hanging in an exhibit at a gallery. Upon review, I''m wondering if this would fit more into the "contemporary" category.  Doesn''t really matter because it''s a discussion that can go on ad infinitum.</td>', 'Is that Freddy Krueger in the lower left? LOL I like the tulip theme that runs throughout.  This is bizarre and certainly befitting of the Fine Art category.  I can see this hanging in an exhibit at a gallery. Upon review, I''m wondering if this would fit more into the "contemporary" category.  Doesn''t really matter because it''s a discussion that can go on ad infinitum.', '2011-04-09 12:19:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380380, 945244, 115307, '<td valign="top">I love the editing on this. So dark and gloomy, but in an appealing way. I also love the contrast between the door and the person, the visual weight is on the door, which just further brings home the point you are trying to convey. 7</td>', 'I love the editing on this. So dark and gloomy, but in an appealing way. I also love the contrast between the door and the person, the visual weight is on the door, which just further brings home the point you are trying to convey. 7', '2011-04-09 12:42:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6380385, 944611, 115307, '<td valign="top">Love the picture, absolutely hate the border. Could you really see any piece of fine art with a border like that? The matching splotches on the person and wall are very interesting and I love the painterly feel. 6</td>', 'Love the picture, absolutely hate the border. Could you really see any piece of fine art with a border like that? The matching splotches on the person and wall are very interesting and I love the painterly feel. 6', '2011-04-09 12:47:01.000000', NULL, 1),
