(6392842, 944750, 65319, '<td valign="top">Since I''m not allowed to shop at IKEA, I browsed the <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30364" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ubique</a> Boutique today, and I was delighted to rediscover this one as one of my favs:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=918031" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1296/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_918031.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1296/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_918031.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1296/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_918031.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>However, Paul, I must confess to you that your image "Mekong" completely puzzles and baffles me:<br/> <br/>I stared and stared at this image for a long time and tried to align my inner vision so that I too may enjoy the delights of what the Jury found so enticing. I read all the notes and I''m feeling completely awkward to ask anyone to explain this image to me. So, I''ve resolved myself now to make peace with the pieces of this puzzle with the faith that one day the mysteries will be revealed even to one such as me.<br/> <br/>But, the horse photo...I want to take that one home! :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-04-22 20:48:18.</i></td>', 'Since I''m not allowed to shop at IKEA, I browsed the  Ubique Boutique today, and I was delighted to rediscover this one as one of my favs:   However, Paul, I must confess to you that your image "Mekong" completely puzzles and baffles me: I stared and stared at this image for a long time and tried to align my inner vision so that I too may enjoy the delights of what the Jury found so enticing. I read all the notes and I''m feeling completely awkward to ask anyone to explain this image to me. So, I''ve resolved myself now to make peace with the pieces of this puzzle with the faith that one day the mysteries will be revealed even to one such as me. But, the horse photo...I want to take that one home! :-)', '2011-04-22 12:32:44.000000', '2011-04-22 21:48:18.000000', 0),
(6392922, 944750, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hihosilver:</b></div><hr/><i> I confess this image puzzles me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you!</td>', 'Originally posted by hihosilver: I confess this image puzzles me.  Thank you!', '2011-04-22 13:47:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6393169, 945150, 16106, '<td valign="top">I always try to leave a note for the image that I rated highly that finished lowest in the voting, and in this challenge this entry has that dubious distinction.<br/> <br/>I think you were done in by the voter''s notion of "fine". I could easily see this being hung in a modernist museum, with its spiraling questions of how an image represents reality, how letters and symbols stand for a concrete objects, how pigment on paper comes to take on the meaning of a depicted object, and how labels themselves shift our understanding of an object. It just goes ''round and ''round. Ouroboros eating his own tail.<br/> <br/>Plus the image itself is just eccentric fun.<br/> <br/>Congratulations, and Im sorry.</td>', 'I always try to leave a note for the image that I rated highly that finished lowest in the voting, and in this challenge this entry has that dubious distinction. I think you were done in by the voter''s notion of "fine". I could easily see this being hung in a modernist museum, with its spiraling questions of how an image represents reality, how letters and symbols stand for a concrete objects, how pigment on paper comes to take on the meaning of a depicted object, and how labels themselves shift our understanding of an object. It just goes ''round and ''round. Ouroboros eating his own tail. Plus the image itself is just eccentric fun. Congratulations, and Im sorry.', '2011-04-22 20:37:18.000000', NULL, 0),
